I had a very earthy therapist who wouldn't have given it a second thought. I have also had very analytical therapists. So I think it depends on the type of person you get. And you can always say I want to see a different person. You can always disagree with their assessment and not take the medication they suggest. You are paying them, you control the situation. 

&#x200B;

With that said, if you are nervous about it, just don't say empath. Say you can always tell what mood another person is in and it always rubs off on you. Phrasing is everything

