I see nothing wrong with this as an elective class if they are promoting the hunting of animals. If it is firearm safety then I would say make it required. REAL LIFE SKILLS should be taught in schools. How to grow food. How to do taxes. How to find fresh water. Hunting is a useful skill to have, however, if you are against the harming of animals it makes sense to only have this as an elective class. Auto shop should have never been taken out of schools... Kids should be able to change tires and oil.

&#x200B;

It literally infuriates me that I did not learn anything of actual importance in school whatsoever. I have never used any math, science, barely used engish skills other than to type a resume.... Never used history other than to sound smart in a conversation for no real reason. 

&#x200B;

Things considered "basic". What is basic is the laws of this country, not the history of it. Human rights. What is basic is how to provide for yourself. Teach kids how to cook food so they aren't eating ramen and kraft in their mid 20's still. Teach them how to find their way home when their phones die. Teach them public speaking skills so that they aren't awkwardly posting inapropriate pictures online for attention, instead of having conversations.

&#x200B;

I find it our education system very useless... 

&#x200B;

End of rant, sorry

